[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Bloc and Cubit Architecture in Flutter"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"State management is one of the most critical aspects of building scalable Flutter applications. The BLoC (Business Logic Component) pattern helps to separate business logic from the presentation layer, making your code testable, maintainable, and predictable."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Cubit vs. Bloc"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Flutter provides two main approaches within the bloc package: Cubit and Bloc. A Cubit is a simpler, function-based state manager where you call functions directly to emit new states. A Bloc is event-driven, meaning you convert incoming events into outgoing states using reactive streams (Event-to-State transformation)."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 1: Setting up Dependencies"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"To get started, add the flutter_bloc package to your pubspec.yaml file alongside the core bloc library."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"dependencies:
  flutter:
    sdk: flutter
  flutter_bloc: ^8.1.3
  bloc: ^8.1.2"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 2: Creating a Cubit Implementation"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Let us implement a simple counter Cubit. First, define the state and the Cubit class with methods that trigger state changes."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"import 'package:flutter_bloc/flutter_bloc.dart';

class CounterCubit extends Cubit<int> {
  CounterCubit() : super(0);

  void increment() => emit(state + 1);
  void decrement() => emit(state - 1);
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 3: Creating a Bloc Implementation"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"For more complex features, use a Bloc. You must define explicit Event classes, State classes, and map those events to states using EventHandler registrations."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"import 'package:flutter_bloc/flutter_bloc.dart';

// Events
abstract class CounterEvent {}
class IncrementEvent extends CounterEvent {}
class DecrementEvent extends CounterEvent {}

// Bloc
class CounterBloc extends Bloc<CounterEvent, int> {
  CounterBloc() : super(0) {
    on<IncrementEvent>((event, emit) => emit(state + 1));
    on<DecrementEvent>((event, emit) => emit(state - 1));
  }
}"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 4: Providing and Consuming the State in UI"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Use BlocProvider to inject your Cubit or Bloc down the widget tree, and BlocBuilder to rebuild parts of your UI in response to state updates."},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"class CounterPage extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return BlocProvider(
      create: (_) => CounterCubit(),
      child: Scaffold(
        appBar: AppBar(title: Text('Cubit Counter')),
        body: Center(
          child: BlocBuilder<CounterCubit, int>(
            builder: (context, count) {
              return Text('Count: $count', style: TextStyle(fontSize: 24));
            },
          ),
        ),
        floatingActionButton: Column(
          mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.end,
          children: [
            FloatingActionButton(
              onPressed: () => context.read<CounterCubit>().increment(),
              child: Icon(Icons.add),
            ),
            SizedBox(height: 8),
            FloatingActionButton(
              onPressed: () => context.read<CounterCubit>().decrement(),
              child: Icon(Icons.remove),
            ),
          ],
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}"},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices"},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Keep states immutable by using packages like Freezed or implementing copyWith methods."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use Cubit for simple state transitions and UI toggles; reserve Bloc for complex workflows with multiple event triggers."},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Leverage BlocObserver to log state transitions globally for debugging purposes."}]
